WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.804 align:start position:0% line:0%
Today, we're
in Shawnee, Oklahoma.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.306 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
More specifically,
we're at the Potawatomi
Nation bird aviary,

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:09.475 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
where they've
got some eagles, hawks,
even hummingbirds.

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:12.478 align:start position:0%
So we're gonna film
a variety of wings,
big and small,

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:14.580 align:start position:0%
in super slow mo.
The downside is,

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.416 align:start position:0%
it's raining
and it's quite dark,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.551 align:start position:0%
so we're gonna have
to wait for some holes
in these clouds,

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start position:0%
but hopefully, we'll get
some lovely-looking footage.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Why don't we go
  and meet the people?
- Quickly, it's raining.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start position:0%
It's raining, yeah.

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:35.201 align:start position:0%
Hi. Great to meet you, Jennifer.
Bree, how's it going?

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.469
- Good to have you here.
- Very nice to meet you.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.171 line:0%
So what is it that
you guys do here?

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.540 align:start position:0% line:0%
- What are you responsible for?
- Well, we are humbled

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.675
to be able to care for
these wonderful eagles here.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.445
All these eagles you meet here
have been injured in some way.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.113
So we need to take care
of them now.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.514
They can't take care of
themselves out in the wild.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:49.816
Dan: That's really good.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.551
What other kind of birds
do you have here?

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:52.819 size:81% position:41%
We have falcons and hawks,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.455 align:start position:0%
and then we have
a golden eagle also.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.357 align:start size:81% position:19%
I've been told you've also
got hummingbirds, as well,
not just birds of prey.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:72% position:28%
Are they a part of this
or are they--

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.360 align:start size:56% position:44%
They are just
wild hummingbirds.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start position:0%
But we're lucky enough
to have them come visit here.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.532
We have planted specific
plants for pollinators--

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.534
monarchs, hummingbirds,
so I think that helps, too.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.370 align:start size:66% position:34%
We've also stopped
spraying, so we don't
use any pesticides

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:13.239 align:start size:81% position:19%
or any chemicals down here
that would be harmful,

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.541 align:start size:81% position:19%
so there's an ample supply
of things they need.

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:17.376 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh, sweet.
- All right, I think we should

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:18.711 size:88% position:44%
wait for it to stop raining,

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.279 align:start position:0%
and then we'll go
and film some birds.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:23.149 line:0%
- So, who's this guy?
- His name is Nikon.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start position:0% line:0%
This is actually
we call an Augur Buzzard,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start position:0%
so he's a relative
of red-tailed hawks,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:91% position:9%
- kinda like their cousin.
- Cool tips.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start position:0%
He's gonna do
what we call rousing.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:63% position:38%
See all his feathers
puffing out.

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:33.726 align:start position:0%
All birds do this.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.561 align:start position:0%
It means he's very
happy right now,

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:36.729 size:75% position:38%
so he must like you two.

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:88% position:13%
Why haven't you
never roused for me?

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:41.467 align:start size:78% position:22%
Sorry, I don't really
know what to say to that.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.569 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think it would be cool
to start with a shot

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:88% position:13%
where he's coming
right at the camera,

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause then we'll see him
braking and putting
his feet forward.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Let's try that.
- Yeah, let's try that.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.550 align:start size:59% position:41%
That's pretty good.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.127
Gav:
<i> Look at that. Wow.</i>

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:15.601
Dan:<i> They all just look so easy
 and quick in real time,</i>

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.603
<i> but then when you see it
 in slow-motion--</i>

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:18.905
Gav:
<i> It's an absolute operation.</i>

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.607
Dan:
<i> Yeah, there's so much to it.</i>

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.912
<i> He sticks his feet out first.
 Puts the brakes on.</i>

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> - Lands.
 - That's amazing.</i>

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.618 align:start position:0%
Jennifer: We'll try that
a couple of times.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:33.920 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Are you ready?
- Ready!

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:40.226
- That was cool.
- Are we good?

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:59% position:41%
Yeah, that's great.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.940
Gav:
<i> Wow. That's a leap, as well.</i>

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Dan:<i> Yeah,
 that's a jump, isn't it? </i>
- Gav:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:03.516
Dan:<i> Wow. Look at all the--
 they spread out like fingers.</i>

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.697
<i> He's looking right
 where he's gonna put his feet.</i>

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.880 align:start size:53% position:47%
That was amazing.

00:03:34.913 --> 00:03:36.315 align:start position:0%
All right, Bree,
who's this fella?

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start position:0%
This Miata Bay.
This is out golden eagle.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.852 align:start position:0% line:0%
Usually, when we put him
out on a perch,

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:40.953 size:84% position:42% line:0%
he'll give us a good rouse.

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.521 align:start position:0% line:0%
So if you guys
wanna try that out?

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.424
Yeah, I'll get
a slow mo rouse.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.796 align:start position:0%
He seems really tame.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:52.698 align:start position:0%
He's been with us since
he was about a year old,

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.901 align:start position:0%
so he's really
accustomed to people.

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:59.906 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Go on.
- Look at his feathers.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.709
I got it.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:17.924
Gav:<i> Huh. He actually shed
 quite a lot of small bits.</i>

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.030
Dan:
<i> It looks like he's in a fan.</i>

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.732 align:start size:78% position:22%
It doesn't even look like
he's doing it to himself.

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:28.768 align:start size:56% position:44%
It just looks like
it's really windy.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:30.870 align:start size:13% position:88%
Wow.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:34.974
Gav:
<i> Pretty impressive dexterity</i>

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:36.075
<i> over all those
 different feathers.</i>

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:37.410
Dan:
<i> It looks so fluid.</i>

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.645
Gav:
<i> Yeah. That was cool.</i>

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.781 size:88% position:56%
How close can we get to him?

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.416 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, would I be able to get
a close-up of his face?

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.051 align:start position:0%
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, you're fine.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.619 size:75% position:38%
Watch your feet.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.890 align:start position:0%
Okay, let's zoom
right in on him here.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.628 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think that was his blink.
- Yeah.

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.430
Gav: Let's have
a look at that.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.699 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Oh, that's weird.
- Do you wanna see this?

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.001 align:start size:66% position:34%
- Yeah.
- Oh, man.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.603 align:start position:0%
Okay, ready?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.610 align:start size:44% position:56%
That is crazy.

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:14.947 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Oh, my God.
- Dan:<i> It actually pauses.</i>

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.117
<i> It's closed,
 and then it's open again.</i>

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.086
Gav:
<i> It looks like a dinosaur.</i>

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.787
Dan:
<i> That's just one at a time.</i>

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.724
-<i> It's so weird. </i>
- Bree:<i> Oh, my God.</i>

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.959
- Gav:<i> Isn't that crazy? </i>
- Dan:<i> That is mental.</i>

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:28.794
<i> And they don't even close
 and open at the same time.</i>

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:30.629
 Gav:<i> You can actually--
'cause of the angle of the eye,</i>

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:31.964
<i> you can see it
 like a curtain coming around.</i>

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.333
Bree:
<i> Yeah, it comes around.</i>

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.372
Gav:<i> It's so crazy.
 I could film this all day.</i>

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.841 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So that's his inner eyelid.
- Mm-hmm.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:45.644 align:start position:0%
So when they're
hunting and flying,
you know, they can just--

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:47.480 align:start position:0%
- it just keeps their eye moist.
- And it's thin enough

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.415
- for them to see through.
- They can see through it.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.818 align:start size:63% position:38%
So this seems to be
a pretty active bush
for hummingbirds.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:56.756 size:81% position:59%
So we've set up the 25/11
at 28,500 frames a second,

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.891 align:start size:88% position:13%
and have attached
a really long trigger cable.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:02.995 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we'll get out the way,
and hopefully when we leave,

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:03.996 align:start size:81% position:19%
they'll come back and eat.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.032 size:78% position:39%
And action, hummingbirds.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.435 size:81% position:41%
Got Dan on the binoculars.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.638
Dan: No.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.510 align:start position:0%
Gav: Look, there's one
there, that-- oh.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.844 align:start size:69% position:31%
All right, go on, son.
Go on, son.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:20.579 align:start size:78% position:22%
Get in there. Go on, son.

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:23.116 align:start size:75% position:25%
Yeah, you can trigger it
now any time.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.723 align:start position:0%
All right, take five,
hummingbirds.

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:33.393
Gav:<i> Wow.</i>

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.862
<i> Even though
 it's out of focus,</i>

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:39.698
<i> the very tip of the wing
 is in focus.</i>

00:06:39.731 --> 00:06:41.667
Dan:
<i> 'Cause the focus is so fine
 on this one, isn't it?</i>

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.569
Gav:<i> It's just so shallow.
 Going for the landing.</i>

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:55.881
<i> He did that without moving
 his head an inch.</i>

00:06:55.914 --> 00:06:58.717
Dan:<i> It's weird how they move
 their tails like that
 to stabilize, isn't it?</i>

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.754
Gav:
<i>Yeah, it's causing little gusts
 of wind on his back feathers.</i>

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:07.726
<i> Oh, it's insane.
They're just moving their wings
 around so quick.</i>

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:11.063
<i> It's almost like
 he's steering his shoulders</i>

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.065
<i> and the head and body
 are just like--</i>

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:16.569 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> they just follow along. </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.204
<i> We got him feeding there
 in mid-air.</i>

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:21.073
Gav:<i> Didn't bother landing.
 Oh, that's cool.</i>

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:23.976 align:start size:72% position:28%
All right, two Phantoms
at once, shall we?

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:26.846 align:start position:0%
So this one is
much higher resolution,
but not nearly as fast.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.915 align:start position:0%
Doesn't take them long
to come back, does it?

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:31.750
Dan:
No, they quickly see
that you're gone

00:07:31.783 --> 00:07:33.786 align:start position:0%
and start trying
to feed again.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:34.920
Gav: He's checking them
all out.

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:37.757 align:start position:0%
Yeah. Yeah!

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.828 align:start position:0%
All right, trigger it.
Not sure what we'll get there.

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.935 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Gav:<i> Oh, look at that. </i>
-<i> Whoa. Whoa!</i>

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:51.504
Gav:<i> He just is not
 happy about it.</i>

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:54.607
Dan:<i> Dive-bombs him.
 Let him feed.</i>

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.141
Gav:<i> He's not having it.</i>

00:07:56.174 --> 00:07:57.943
Dan:<i> He's looking at
 the other one, thinking,</i>

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.578
<i> "Am I allowed to feed?"</i>

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:01.881
<i> The other one was like,
 "Then I'll feed."</i>

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.582
Gav:<i> Well,
 I saw it in real time</i>

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:04.917
<i> and it just looked like
 playing or something.</i>

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.252
<i> But in this,
 it looks so violent.</i>

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.120
<i> They're very territorial.</i>

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:10.256
<i> And that beak is a weapon.</i>

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-<i> It's like a little sword. </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.661 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Gav:<i> He's going for it. </i>
-<i> It's all right.
 It's safe, it's safe.</i>

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:19.632
Dan:
<i> Oh, you can see it gulping.</i>

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.767 align:start position:0%
- Gav:<i> That must be his tongue. </i>
-<i> You see that?</i>

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.137
<i> It's properly gulping it down.</i>

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.140 align:start position:0%
That was wicked.
Fun to film. Fun to watch.

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:31.977 align:start position:0%
I don't think there's
any better subject in slow-mo
than animals and nature.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:36.649 align:start size:91% position:9%
- It's very cool.
- Even the eagle blinking,
  it was so alien-looking.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:40.152 align:start position:0%
There's white curtains
coming from the under eyelids
sweeping over.

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:42.821 align:start size:78% position:22%
So cool that
they can see through that
when they're flying.

00:08:42.854 --> 00:08:44.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- It has a real-- yeah.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:45.658 size:78% position:39%
I'm blown away, honestly.

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:46.992 align:start position:0%
Hopefully,
you enjoyed that video.

00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:49.194 align:start position:0%
Feel free to subscribe
to the Slow Mo Guys,

00:08:49.227 --> 00:08:53.832
and click over here
